      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تسفّد فَرَسَهُ</span></b>  <i>He mounted his mare from behind;</i> (M;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استسفدها</span></b> : (AAF, M:) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَعِيرَهُ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استسفد</span></b>  <i>he came to his camel from behind,
and mounted him:</i> (IAar, K:) and [in like manner] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تسفّدَهُ</span> <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعَرْقَبَهُ</span>, (K,) i. e. <i>he mounted him
from behind.</i> (TA.)

